@*
    REQ-UI-045 / REQ-UI-046 / REQ-UI-047 / REQ-UI-048 / REQ-UI-049 — Phase effort, the seventh report
    page and the TechieFlow branch of `/effort`.

    Everything here binds `AnalysisResult.Phases` — a `PhaseEffortAnalysis` — and the ADR-026 wrapper
    types are the point of the screen rather than an inconvenience it works around:

      1. `TokenWindow` carries `MeasuredN` and `UnmeasuredN` beside the figure, so every token surface
         prints `measured on n of N runs` as VISIBLE TEXT and never as a tooltip (BRD-146).
      2. `FanoutObservation` carries `ObservedN`, `UnobservedNotTree` and `UnobservedPredatesField`.
         The two exclusions are published two ways and are never pooled, because they have different
         futures — "we did not look" can change tomorrow, "we could not have looked" never will
         (BRD-147). A phase with no observed run reads `not observed`; it NEVER reads `0 subagents`,
         which would turn an absence of observation into a measurement (TF-005, ADR-026).
      3. `share_of_duration` and `share_of_tokens_out` are the oracle's own strings (`"87%"` / `"—"`)
         and reach the screen unaltered — BRD-152 diffs them as strings (BRD §13).
      4. Dollars are measured per harness and never pooled across harnesses. There is no rate-card
         estimate anywhere on this page, deliberately: an estimated dollar beside a measured one on a
         budgeting screen is how a plausible wrong number gets quoted (BRD-160, BRD-169).
      5. `drifted` is Badge INFO, never destructive. TfLens observes which model ran; it does not
         enforce a routing policy, and a red pill would assert a rule the framework does not have.

    The screen is built to look correct at thin coverage, not merely to survive it: on today's data the
    fan-out coverage tile reads `1 of 13`, and the exclusion card beside it says why. A page that only
    reads well once the data is dense is a page nobody trusts in the meantime.
*@
@page "/effort"
@using System.Globalization
@using TfLens.Core.Metrics
@* Empty and Typography are absent from Components/_Imports.razor's suggested list; a component whose
   namespace is missing degrades to a literal unknown tag with only a warning, so they are named here
   the way Misses.razor and Routing.razor name them. *@
@using TrBlazeUI.Components.Empty
@using TrBlazeUI.Components.Typography
@using TfLens.Components.Shared.Playbook
@implements IDisposable
@inject ITelemetryStore objStore
@inject ShellPreferences objPreferences
@inject ShellState objShellState

<PageTitle>Phase effort · TfLens</PageTitle>

<div class="tflens-stack tflens-effort" data-testid="effort-page">

    @* REQ-UI-045 — the page header and the period filter. *@
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
            <TypographyH2>Phase effort</TypographyH2>
            <TypographyMuted>@Subtitle</TypographyMuted>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" data-testid="effort-period-label">@PeriodLabel</Badge>
            <div class="tflens-period">
                @* TR-020: SelectValue renders the raw bound value until SelectContent has rendered once,
                   so the closed trigger read "all" rather than "All history (default)".
                   DisplayTextSelector is the library's own hook and resolves it without the popover. *@
                <Select TValue="string"
                        Value="@objPeriod"
                        ValueChanged="OnPeriodChangedAsync"
                        DisplayTextSelector="@PeriodTextOf"
                        Class="w-full">
                    <SelectTrigger data-testid="effort-period">
                        <SelectValue Placeholder="All history (default)" />
                    </SelectTrigger>
                    <SelectContent>
                        @foreach (var vOption in PeriodOptions)
                        {
                            <SelectItem TValue="string" Value="@vOption.Key" Text="@vOption.Label">@vOption.Label</SelectItem>
                        }
                    </SelectContent>
                </Select>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* REQ-UI-045 / BRD-169 — the standing budgeting note. It is page copy, never a tooltip, and it is
       not conditional on the data: the framing has to be true of an empty page too. *@
    <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Info" AccentBorder="true" data-testid="effort-budget-note">
        <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="16" />
        <AlertTitle>This is a budgeting view, not a quality scoreboard</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
            <span class="font-mono">*build-phase</span> costing more than
            <span class="font-mono">*log-miss</span> is a fact about what those phases <b>are</b>, not
            evidence that one is inefficient. Quality lives on
            <a class="tflens-link" href="/misses">Misses &amp; rework</a> and
            <a class="tflens-link" href="/coverage">Coverage</a>. There is no per-REQ effort view here and
            there never will be — a run's window divided across the REQs it touched is arithmetic dressed
            as measurement.
        </AlertDescription>
    </Alert>

    @if (IsPlaybook)
    {
        @* REQ-UI-050 — the Playbook axis of /effort is "Phase efficiency" (BRD-162), a different
           component map with its own filters, summary tiles and execution table.

           It is NOT wrapped in PlaybookState. That wrapper decides "is there any Playbook data yet"
           from `PbEvent`, and phase effort is read from the three normalized `PbPhase*` tables the
           schema-2 exporter writes — a workspace can have every phase row and no `PbEvent` at all.
           Gating this surface on the event count would hide a populated screen, and worse, would hide
           the BRD-163 unsupported banner behind an empty state that names the wrong cause. The
           standing axis note is rendered directly instead, and the surface reads its own report. *@
        <PlaybookAxisNote />
        <PlaybookEffortSurface UserId="@objUserId" />
    }
    else if (!objIsLoaded)
    {
        <Card>
            <CardContent Class="p-6">
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                    <Skeleton Class="h-4 w-full" />
                    <Skeleton Class="h-4 w-3/4" />
                    <Skeleton Class="h-4 w-1/2" />
                </div>
            </CardContent>
        </Card>
    }
    else if (objLoadError is not null)
    {
        <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Danger" AccentBorder="true" data-testid="effort-error">
            @* TR-008: 2.0.0 ships only the post-rename Lucide names — `alert-triangle` renders nothing. *@
            <LucideIcon Name="triangle-alert" Size="16" />
            <AlertTitle>Couldn't build the effort view</AlertTitle>
            <AlertDescription>@objLoadError</AlertDescription>
        </Alert>
    }
    else if (objPhases.RunsLive == 0)
    {
        <Empty Title="No runs recorded yet"
               Description="@EmptyDescription"
               data-testid="effort-empty">
            <Icon>
                <LucideIcon Name="gauge" Size="32" />
            </Icon>
        </Empty>
    }
    else
    {
        @* ---- BAND 1 — the KPI row (REQ-UI-046) -------------------------------------------------

           StatGroup is not used here and the reason is arithmetic: its shim spans tiles on TrBlazeUI's
           own 12-column grid, and twelve does not divide by five, so a five-tile row lands 4 + 1. The
           approved design puts five equal tiles across at 1280 and one per row at 390, so this row is
           the page's own grid and the tiles stand alone inside it (TR-002 — the library ships no
           responsive grid utilities, so the breakpoints are real media queries in the scoped sheet). *@
        <div class="tflens-effort-kpis" data-testid="effort-kpis">

            <StatTile Title="Runs recorded"
                      Value="@CountText(objPhases.RunsLive)"
                      IconName="activity"
                      Accent="StatAccent.Chart1"
                      data-testid="kpi-runs">
                <DescriptionContent>
                    live records in <span class="font-mono">runs.jsonl</span> · backfilled rows are
                    excluded and reported separately
                </DescriptionContent>
            </StatTile>

            @* REQ-UI-046 — the wall-clock sub-line says in words that this is never human effort. *@
            <StatTile Title="Total wall clock"
                      Value="@DurationText(objPhases.DurationSecondsTotal)"
                      IconName="clock"
                      Accent="StatAccent.Chart5"
                      data-testid="kpi-wallclock">
                <DescriptionContent>
                    Σ <span class="font-mono">duration_s</span> over @CountText(TimedRuns) timed runs · how
                    long the command windows stayed open, <b>never human effort</b>
                </DescriptionContent>
            </StatTile>

            @* REQ-UI-046 / BRD-146 — `measured on n of N runs` as visible text, never a tooltip. *@
            <StatTile Title="Output tokens"
                      Value="@TokenText(objPhases.TokensOutTotal)"
                      IconName="database"
                      Accent="StatAccent.Chart2"
                      data-testid="kpi-tokens-out">
                <DescriptionContent>
                    <b data-testid="kpi-tokens-measured">measured on @TokensMeasuredRuns of @objPhases.RunsLive runs</b>
                    · @CountText(TokensUnmeasuredRuns) runs carry no token window and are excluded, never
                    averaged in as zero
                </DescriptionContent>
            </StatTile>

            <StatTile Title="Heaviest phase"
                      IconName="layers"
                      Accent="StatAccent.Chart3"
                      data-testid="kpi-heaviest">
                <ValueContent>
                    <span class="tflens-kpi-cmd font-mono">@HeaviestCmd</span>
                </ValueContent>
                <DescriptionContent>
                    @HeaviestSummary
                </DescriptionContent>
            </StatTile>

            @* REQ-UI-046 / BRD-151 — fan-out coverage is a COVERAGE figure and it sits on the KPI row
               rather than being buried, because every fan-out number further down is bounded by it. *@
            <StatTile Title="Fan-out coverage"
                      Value="@($"{objPhases.FanoutObservedN} of {objPhases.RunsLive}")"
                      IconName="git-fork"
                      Accent="StatAccent.Chart4"
                      Class="tflens-kpi-accent"
                      data-testid="kpi-fanout-coverage">
                <DescriptionContent>
                    runs whose window actually observed subagents (@PercentText(objPhases.FanoutObservedN, objPhases.RunsLive)).
                    A coverage figure, deliberately on the KPI row — every fan-out number below is bounded by it
                </DescriptionContent>
            </StatTile>
        </div>

        @* ---- BAND 2 — the denominators (BRD-146, BRD-147, BRD-148) ------------------------------ *@
        <h3 class="tflens-band-heading">What is excluded, and why</h3>
        <div class="tflens-effort-denominators" data-testid="effort-denominators">

            <Card Class="h-full" data-testid="effort-token-window">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                        <div class="min-w-0">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Token window</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>A run with no token window is not a run that spent nothing</CardDescription>
                        </div>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" Class="tflens-nowrap-badge">
                            @TokensMeasuredRuns of @objPhases.RunsLive measured
                        </Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    <div class="tflens-table">
                        @* TR-009: ShowPagination="false" hides the pager but still truncates to
                           InitialPageSize, so the page size has to cover every row or rows vanish. *@
                        <DataTable TData="ScopeRow"
                                   Data="@ScopeRows"
                                   ShowToolbar="false"
                                   ShowPagination="false"
                                   InitialPageSize="50"
                                   AriaLabel="Runs by token scope"
                                   data-testid="effort-scope-table">
                            <Columns>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="ScopeRow" TValue="string"
                                                 Property="@(aRow => aRow.Scope)" Header="Bucket">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                        <span class="font-mono @(vRow.IsUnmeasured ? "text-muted-foreground" : string.Empty)">@vRow.Scope</span>
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="ScopeRow" TValue="int"
                                                 Property="@(aRow => aRow.Runs)" Header="Runs"
                                                 CellClass="text-right">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                        <span class="tabular-nums @(vRow.IsUnmeasured ? "font-semibold" : string.Empty)"
                                              data-testid="@($"scope-{vRow.TestKey}")">@CountText(vRow.Runs)</span>
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="ScopeRow" TValue="string"
                                                 Property="@(aRow => aRow.Meaning)" Header="What it means">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                        <span class="tflens-small @(vRow.IsUnmeasured ? "text-muted-foreground" : string.Empty)">@vRow.Meaning</span>
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                            </Columns>
                        </DataTable>
                    </div>
                </CardContent>
                <CardFooter Class="tflens-card-note">
                    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                        <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="16" />
                        Every token tile carries
                        <b><span class="font-mono">measured on n of N runs</span></b> as visible text, never
                        as a tooltip. Below <span class="font-mono">MIN_N = @MetricsConstants.MinN</span> a
                        per-run figure renders <i>insufficient data (n=…)</i> and never
                        <span class="font-mono">0</span>.
                    </p>
                </CardFooter>
            </Card>

            @* BRD-147 — the two exclusions, published two ways and never pooled. *@
            <Card Class="h-full" data-testid="effort-fanout-exclusions">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                        <div class="min-w-0">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Fan-out observation</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>Two different facts, published two ways and never pooled</CardDescription>
                        </div>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline"
                               Class="tflens-badge-warning tflens-nowrap-badge"
                               data-testid="effort-observed-badge">@objPhases.FanoutObservedN observed</Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    <div class="tflens-table tflens-kv-table">
                        <DataTable TData="ExclusionRow"
                                   Data="@ExclusionRows"
                                   ShowToolbar="false"
                                   ShowPagination="false"
                                   InitialPageSize="50"
                                   AriaLabel="Fan-out observation and its two exclusions"
                                   data-testid="effort-fanout-table">
                            <Columns>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="ExclusionRow" TValue="string"
                                                 Property="@(aRow => aRow.Label)" Header="Bucket">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                        <div>
                                            @if (vRow.IsObservedRow)
                                            {
                                                <b>@vRow.Label</b>
                                            }
                                            else
                                            {
                                                <span class="font-mono">@vRow.Label</span>
                                            }
                                            <div class="tflens-xs text-muted-foreground">@vRow.Meaning</div>
                                        </div>
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="ExclusionRow" TValue="int"
                                                 Property="@(aRow => aRow.Runs)" Header="Share">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                        <span class="tflens-bar">
                                            <Progress Value="@vRow.Percent" Class="h-2" IndicatorClass="@vRow.FillClass" />
                                        </span>
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="ExclusionRow" TValue="string"
                                                 Property="@(aRow => aRow.Text)" Header="Runs"
                                                 CellClass="text-right">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                        <span class="tabular-nums tflens-nowrap" data-testid="@($"fanout-{vRow.TestKey}")">
                                            @if (vRow.IsObservedRow)
                                            {
                                                <b>@CountText(vRow.Runs)</b>
                                            }
                                            else
                                            {
                                                @CountText(vRow.Runs)
                                            }
                                            · @PercentText(vRow.Runs, objPhases.RunsLive)
                                        </span>
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                            </Columns>
                        </DataTable>
                    </div>
                </CardContent>
                <CardFooter Class="tflens-card-note">
                    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                        <b>Pooling these two would be the defect.</b> A <span class="font-mono">main</span>-scope
                        window never read a subagent transcript at all, so coercing its absent
                        <span class="font-mono">subagent_runs</span> to <span class="font-mono">0</span> reports
                        <i>“this phase spawns no subagents”</i> when the truth is <i>“we did not look.”</i> The
                        <span class="font-mono">FIELD_SINCE</span> floor carries
                        <span class="font-mono">subagent_runs</span>,
                        <span class="font-mono">tokens_out_subagents</span> and
                        <span class="font-mono">model_tokens_out</span> at
                        <span class="font-mono">@FieldSince</span>, in the same table and the same code path as
                        <span class="font-mono">LATE_GATES</span>.
                    </p>
                </CardFooter>
            </Card>
        </div>

        @* ---- BAND 3 — the phase table (REQ-UI-047) --------------------------------------------- *@
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3">
            <div>
                <h3 class="tflens-band-heading">Command phase</h3>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                    One row per <span class="font-mono">cmd</span>, sorted by share of output tokens.
                    <b>Measured</b> is a column, not a footnote.
                </p>
            </div>
            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" Class="tflens-nowrap-badge">
                @objPhases.Phases.Count phases · @objPhases.RunsLive runs
            </Badge>
        </div>

        <Card data-testid="effort-phases">
            <CardContent Class="pt-6">
                <div class="tflens-table">
                    <DataTable TData="PhaseTableRow"
                               Data="@PhaseTableRows"
                               ShowToolbar="false"
                               ShowPagination="false"
                               InitialPageSize="200"
                               AriaLabel="Effort by command phase"
                               data-testid="effort-phase-table">
                        <Columns>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseTableRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Cmd)" Header="Command phase">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="font-mono" data-testid="@($"phase-cmd-{vRow.Key}")">@vRow.Cmd</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseTableRow" TValue="int"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Runs)" Header="Runs" CellClass="text-right">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="tabular-nums">@CountText(vRow.Runs)</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseTableRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.WallClock)" Header="Wall clock" CellClass="text-right">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="tabular-nums tflens-nowrap">@vRow.WallClock</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseTableRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Median)" Header="Median" CellClass="text-right">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="tabular-nums tflens-nowrap">@vRow.Median</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            @* BRD-152 — the oracle's own share string, rendered and never reformatted. *@
                            <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseTableRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.ShareOfDuration)" Header="Share of time"
                                             CellClass="text-right">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="tabular-nums">@vRow.ShareOfDuration</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseTableRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.TokensOut)" Header="Output tokens"
                                             CellClass="text-right">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="tabular-nums tflens-nowrap" title="@vRow.TokensOutExact">@vRow.TokensOut</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseTableRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.ShareOfTokensOut)" Header="Share of output"
                                             CellClass="text-right">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <b class="tabular-nums" data-testid="@($"phase-share-{vRow.Key}")">@vRow.ShareOfTokensOut</b>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            @* REQ-UI-047 / BRD-151 — Measured is a COLUMN. *@
                            <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseTableRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Measured)" Header="Measured"
                                             CellClass="text-right">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="tabular-nums tflens-nowrap" data-testid="@($"phase-measured-{vRow.Key}")">@vRow.Measured</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                            @* ADR-026 — `not observed`, never `0 subagents`. *@
                            <DataTableColumn TData="PhaseTableRow" TValue="string"
                                             Property="@(aRow => aRow.Fanout)" Header="Fan-out"
                                             CellClass="text-right">
                                <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                    <span class="tabular-nums tflens-nowrap @(vRow.IsFanoutObserved ? string.Empty : "text-muted-foreground")"
                                          data-testid="@($"phase-fanout-{vRow.Key}")">@vRow.Fanout</span>
                                </CellTemplate>
                            </DataTableColumn>
                        </Columns>
                    </DataTable>
                </div>
            </CardContent>
            <CardFooter Class="tflens-card-note">
                <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                    <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="16" />
                    The dimension is the <b>command phase</b> — the producer's
                    <span class="font-mono">cmd</span> is a slash command, and one command can contain
                    several lifecycle stages (<span class="font-mono">*build-phase</span> covers build
                    <i>and</i> self-smoke). A window is never split between conceptual phases by token
                    proportion, and a <b>whole-task total is unavailable</b> without an explicit cohort — a
                    reused session is not one.
                </p>
            </CardFooter>
        </Card>

        @* ---- BAND 4 — per-phase detail (REQ-UI-048) -------------------------------------------- *@
        <h3 class="tflens-band-heading">Per-phase detail</h3>
        <div class="tflens-detail-stack" data-testid="effort-phase-detail">
            @foreach (var vRow in objPhases.Phases)
            {
                var vKey = KeyOf(vRow.Cmd);
                var vIsOpen = objOpenPhases.Contains(vRow.Cmd);

                <Card Class="tflens-detail" data-testid="@($"effort-detail-{vKey}")">
                    <Collapsible Open="@vIsOpen" OpenChanged="@(aOpen => OnPhaseToggled(vRow.Cmd, aOpen))">
                        <CollapsibleTrigger>
                            <span class="tflens-detail-trigger" data-testid="@($"effort-detail-trigger-{vKey}")">
                                <LucideIcon Name="@(vIsOpen ? "chevron-down" : "chevron-right")" Size="16" />
                                <span class="font-mono">@vRow.Cmd</span>
                                <span class="text-muted-foreground">— @TriggerSummary(vRow)</span>
                                <span class="tflens-spacer"></span>
                                <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" Class="tflens-nowrap-badge">@ObservationBadge(vRow)</Badge>
                            </span>
                        </CollapsibleTrigger>
                        <CollapsibleContent>
                            @* TR-018: a closed CollapsibleContent still lays its children out and overlaps
                               what follows, so the subtree is guarded rather than merely hidden. *@
                            @if (vIsOpen)
                            {
                                <div class="tflens-detail-body">

                                    @* --- 1 · Time --- *@
                                    <div class="tflens-panel">
                                        <div class="tflens-panel-label">1 · Time</div>
                                        <div class="tflens-quad">
                                            <div>
                                                <div class="tflens-xs text-muted-foreground">Total</div>
                                                <div class="tflens-figure" data-testid="@($"time-total-{vKey}")">@PhaseTotalText(vRow)</div>
                                            </div>
                                            <div>
                                                <div class="tflens-xs text-muted-foreground">Median run</div>
                                                <div class="tflens-figure">@SecondsText(vRow.Duration.MedianSeconds)</div>
                                            </div>
                                            <div>
                                                <div class="tflens-xs text-muted-foreground">Longest run</div>
                                                <div class="tflens-figure">@SecondsText(vRow.Duration.MaxSeconds)</div>
                                            </div>
                                            <div>
                                                <div class="tflens-xs text-muted-foreground">Share of all wall clock</div>
                                                <div class="tflens-figure">@vRow.ShareOfDuration</div>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                        <p class="tflens-xs text-muted-foreground">
                                            Wall-clock elapsed is how long the command window stayed open. It is
                                            not active time and it is <b>never</b> human effort — nobody sat
                                            watching for @PhaseTotalText(vRow), and TfLens will not imply that
                                            they did. @TimedRunsNote(vRow)
                                        </p>
                                    </div>

                                    @* --- 2 · Tokens --- BRD-146: the band label carries its own denominator. *@
                                    <div class="tflens-panel">
                                        <div class="tflens-panel-label">
                                            2 · Tokens
                                            <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" Class="tflens-nowrap-badge tflens-panel-badge"
                                                   data-testid="@($"tokens-measured-{vKey}")">
                                                measured on @vRow.TokensMeasuredN of @vRow.Runs runs
                                            </Badge>
                                        </div>
                                        <div class="tflens-panel-table">
                                            <table>
                                                <thead>
                                                    <tr>
                                                        <th>Component</th>
                                                        <th class="tflens-right">Total</th>
                                                        <th class="tflens-right">Median / run</th>
                                                        <th class="tflens-right">Mean / run</th>
                                                    </tr>
                                                </thead>
                                                <tbody>
                                                    <tr>
                                                        <td>Output</td>
                                                        <td class="tflens-right"><b>@TokenTotalText(vRow, vRow.Tokens.Out)</b></td>
                                                        <td class="tflens-right">@TokenFromDouble(vRow.TokensOutMedian)</td>
                                                        @* ADR-007 — the one Figure on this page; below MIN_N it
                                                           refuses to be a number and FigureText prints the refusal. *@
                                                        <td class="tflens-right">
                                                            <FigureText Value="@vRow.TokensOutPerRun.Tokens"
                                                                        Class="tabular-nums"
                                                                        TestId="@($"tokens-mean-{vKey}")" />
                                                        </td>
                                                    </tr>
                                                    <tr>
                                                        <td>Input</td>
                                                        <td class="tflens-right">@TokenTotalText(vRow, vRow.Tokens.In)</td>
                                                        <td class="tflens-right text-muted-foreground">@Dash</td>
                                                        <td class="tflens-right text-muted-foreground">@Dash</td>
                                                    </tr>
                                                    <tr>
                                                        <td>Cache read</td>
                                                        <td class="tflens-right">@TokenTotalText(vRow, vRow.Tokens.CacheRead)</td>
                                                        <td class="tflens-right text-muted-foreground">@Dash</td>
                                                        <td class="tflens-right text-muted-foreground">@Dash</td>
                                                    </tr>
                                                    <tr>
                                                        <td>Cache write</td>
                                                        <td class="tflens-right">@TokenTotalText(vRow, vRow.Tokens.CacheWrite)</td>
                                                        <td class="tflens-right text-muted-foreground">@Dash</td>
                                                        <td class="tflens-right text-muted-foreground">@Dash</td>
                                                    </tr>
                                                </tbody>
                                            </table>
                                        </div>
                                        <p class="tflens-xs text-muted-foreground">
                                            <b>Mean sits beside median, not instead of it.</b> @MeanVersusMedian(vRow)
                                            Only <span class="font-mono">tokens_out</span> carries a per-run figure —
                                            the producer reports the other three as totals over the measured runs, so
                                            a median or a mean for them would be invented here rather than measured.
                                            @UnmeasuredNote(vRow)
                                        </p>
                                    </div>

                                    @* --- 3 · By model --- BRD-150. *@
                                    <div class="tflens-panel">
                                        <div class="tflens-panel-label">3 · By model</div>
                                        @if (vRow.Models.Count == 0)
                                        {
                                            <p class="tflens-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="@($"models-none-{vKey}")">
                                                No run in this phase carried a model attribution — neither a
                                                <span class="font-mono">model_tokens_out</span> split nor a dominant
                                                <span class="font-mono">model</span> label. Not observed, rather than
                                                a phase that ran on no model.
                                            </p>
                                        }
                                        else
                                        {
                                            <div class="tflens-panel-table">
                                                <table>
                                                    <thead>
                                                        <tr>
                                                            <th>Model</th>
                                                            <th class="tflens-right">Runs</th>
                                                            <th class="tflens-right">Output tokens</th>
                                                            <th>Share of this phase</th>
                                                        </tr>
                                                    </thead>
                                                    <tbody>
                                                        @foreach (var vModel in vRow.Models)
                                                        {
                                                            <tr>
                                                                <td><span class="font-mono">@vModel.Model</span></td>
                                                                <td class="tflens-right tabular-nums">@CountText(vModel.Runs)</td>
                                                                <td class="tflens-right tabular-nums">@TokenText(vModel.TokensOut)</td>
                                                                <td>
                                                                    <span class="tflens-bar-row">
                                                                        <span class="tflens-bar">
                                                                            <Progress Value="@Percent(vModel.TokensOut, vRow.Tokens.Out)"
                                                                                      Class="h-2"
                                                                                      IndicatorClass="tflens-fill-1" />
                                                                        </span>
                                                                        <span class="tabular-nums tflens-nowrap">@PercentText(vModel.TokensOut, vRow.Tokens.Out)</span>
                                                                    </span>
                                                                </td>
                                                            </tr>
                                                        }
                                                    </tbody>
                                                </table>
                                            </div>
                                            <p class="tflens-xs text-muted-foreground">
                                                Computed from <span class="font-mono">model_tokens_out</span> — the
                                                per-model <b>split</b>. A mixed-model run's whole window is never
                                                attributed to its dominant <span class="font-mono">model</span>, which
                                                is why the run counts here can exceed the phase's own.
                                                @ModelSourceNote(vRow) <b>This ranking is observational, not
                                                causal</b> — which model gets the hard phases is not random.
                                            </p>
                                        }
                                    </div>

                                    @* --- 4 · Fan-out --- BRD-149: observed_n of runs FIRST, then the numbers. *@
                                    <div class="tflens-panel">
                                        <div class="tflens-panel-label">4 · Fan-out</div>
                                        <Alert Variant="AlertVariant.Warning" Class="tflens-panel-alert"
                                               data-testid="@($"fanout-alert-{vKey}")">
                                            <LucideIcon Name="git-fork" Size="18" />
                                            <AlertTitle>@vRow.Fanout.ObservedN of @vRow.Runs runs observed</AlertTitle>
                                            <AlertDescription>@FanoutCoverageSentence(vRow)</AlertDescription>
                                        </Alert>

                                        @if (vRow.Fanout.IsObserved)
                                        {
                                            <div class="tflens-panel-table tflens-kv-panel">
                                                <table>
                                                    <tbody>
                                                        <tr>
                                                            <td>Spawns, total</td>
                                                            <td class="tflens-right tabular-nums"><b data-testid="@($"spawns-total-{vKey}")">@CountText(vRow.Fanout.SpawnsTotal)</b></td>
                                                            <td class="tflens-small text-muted-foreground">across the @vRow.Fanout.ObservedN observed runs</td>
                                                        </tr>
                                                        <tr>
                                                            <td>Spawns, median / max</td>
                                                            <td class="tflens-right tabular-nums">@SpawnsMedianAndMax(vRow.Fanout)</td>
                                                            <td class="tflens-small text-muted-foreground">per observed run</td>
                                                        </tr>
                                                        <tr>
                                                            <td>Observed runs that spawned anything</td>
                                                            <td class="tflens-right tabular-nums">@vRow.Fanout.RunsWithFanout of @vRow.Fanout.ObservedN</td>
                                                            <td class="tflens-small text-muted-foreground"><span class="font-mono">runs_with_fanout</span></td>
                                                        </tr>
                                                        <tr>
                                                            <td>Subagent output tokens</td>
                                                            <td class="tflens-right tabular-nums">@TokenText(vRow.Fanout.TokensOutSubagents)</td>
                                                            <td class="tflens-small text-muted-foreground"><span class="font-mono">tokens_out_subagents</span> — a count, never a divisor</td>
                                                        </tr>
                                                        <tr>
                                                            <td>Subagent share of output</td>
                                                            <td class="tflens-right tabular-nums">@vRow.Fanout.SubagentShareOfTokensOut</td>
                                                            <td class="tflens-small text-muted-foreground">of the observed runs' measured output</td>
                                                        </tr>
                                                    </tbody>
                                                </table>
                                            </div>
                                        }
                                        else
                                        {
                                            <p class="tflens-xs text-muted-foreground" data-testid="@($"fanout-none-{vKey}")">
                                                <b>Not observed.</b> No run in this phase satisfied
                                                <span class="font-mono">tokens_scope == "tree"</span> and
                                                <span class="font-mono">subagent_runs != null</span>, so there is no
                                                spawn count, no subagent token total and no share to report. The
                                                figure is absent, not zero.
                                            </p>
                                        }

                                        <p class="tflens-xs text-muted-foreground">
                                            <b>Declared vs measured.</b> @DeclaredVersusMeasured(vRow) Both are shown
                                            because they answer different questions: which <i>kinds</i> were invoked
                                            (only the agent knows) versus how many actually ran (only the harness
                                            knows). <b>Where they disagree the measured figure is authoritative</b>,
                                            and the gap is itself a finding about how accurately tasks self-report —
                                            not an error to reconcile away.
                                        </p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            }
                        </CollapsibleContent>
                    </Collapsible>
                </Card>
            }
        </div>

        @* ---- BAND 5 — routing and measured spend (REQ-UI-049, BRD-148, BRD-160) ------------------ *@
        <h3 class="tflens-band-heading">Routing</h3>
        <div class="tflens-effort-lower">

            <Card Class="h-full" data-testid="effort-routing">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                        <div class="min-w-0">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Declared route vs the model that ran</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>Routing is <b>observed</b>, never enforced</CardDescription>
                        </div>
                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline" Class="tflens-nowrap-badge">@objPhases.RunsLive runs</Badge>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    <div class="tflens-table tflens-routing-table">
                        <DataTable TData="RoutingRow"
                                   Data="@RoutingRows"
                                   ShowToolbar="false"
                                   ShowPagination="false"
                                   InitialPageSize="10"
                                   AriaLabel="Routing outcomes"
                                   data-testid="effort-routing-table">
                            <Columns>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="RoutingRow" TValue="string"
                                                 Property="@(aRow => aRow.Outcome)" Header="Outcome">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                        @* REQ-UI-049 — `drifted` is INFO. Drift is made visible, never styled as a
                                           failure: a red pill would assert a routing rule the framework does not
                                           have. TR-016 — BadgeVariant ships no Info/Success member, so the tone
                                           rides on the shared `--alert-*` class from app.css. *@
                                        <Badge Variant="BadgeVariant.Outline"
                                               Class="@($"{vRow.ToneClass} tflens-nowrap-badge")"
                                               data-testid="@($"routing-{vRow.Outcome}")">@vRow.Outcome</Badge>
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="RoutingRow" TValue="int"
                                                 Property="@(aRow => aRow.Runs)" Header="Runs" CellClass="text-right">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                        <span class="tabular-nums" data-testid="@($"routing-count-{vRow.Outcome}")">@CountText(vRow.Runs)</span>
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="RoutingRow" TValue="int"
                                                 Property="@(aRow => aRow.Runs)" Header="Share">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                        <span class="tflens-bar-row">
                                            <span class="tflens-bar">
                                                <Progress Value="@Percent(vRow.Runs, RoutingTotal)" Class="h-2"
                                                          IndicatorClass="@vRow.FillClass" />
                                            </span>
                                            <span class="tabular-nums tflens-nowrap">@PercentText(vRow.Runs, RoutingTotal)</span>
                                        </span>
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="RoutingRow" TValue="string"
                                                 Property="@(aRow => aRow.Meaning)" Header="What it means">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                        <span class="tflens-small text-muted-foreground">@vRow.Meaning</span>
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                            </Columns>
                        </DataTable>
                    </div>

                    @* REQ-UI-049 — the same three counts per phase, which is where the engine holds them.
                       Closed by default so the card face is the design's own three-row summary. *@
                    <div class="tflens-routing-byphase">
                        <Collapsible @bind-Open="objIsRoutingByPhaseOpen">
                            <CollapsibleTrigger>
                                <span class="tflens-detail-trigger" data-testid="effort-routing-byphase-trigger">
                                    <LucideIcon Name="@(objIsRoutingByPhaseOpen ? "chevron-down" : "chevron-right")" Size="16" />
                                    <span class="text-sm font-medium">By command phase</span>
                                </span>
                            </CollapsibleTrigger>
                            <CollapsibleContent>
                                @* TR-018 — guarded, not merely hidden. *@
                                @if (objIsRoutingByPhaseOpen)
                                {
                                    <div class="tflens-panel-table tflens-byphase" data-testid="effort-routing-byphase">
                                        <table>
                                            <thead>
                                                <tr>
                                                    <th>Command phase</th>
                                                    <th class="tflens-right">routed</th>
                                                    <th class="tflens-right">drifted</th>
                                                    <th class="tflens-right">unknown</th>
                                                </tr>
                                            </thead>
                                            <tbody>
                                                @foreach (var vRow in objPhases.Phases)
                                                {
                                                    <tr>
                                                        <td><span class="font-mono">@vRow.Cmd</span></td>
                                                        <td class="tflens-right tabular-nums">@CountText(vRow.Routing.Routed)</td>
                                                        <td class="tflens-right tabular-nums">@CountText(vRow.Routing.Drifted)</td>
                                                        <td class="tflens-right tabular-nums">@CountText(vRow.Routing.Unknown)</td>
                                                    </tr>
                                                }
                                            </tbody>
                                        </table>
                                    </div>
                                }
                            </CollapsibleContent>
                        </Collapsible>
                    </div>
                </CardContent>
                <CardFooter Class="tflens-card-note">
                    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                        <span class="font-mono">drifted</span> is styled as information, never as an error.
                        TfLens observes which model ran; it does not enforce a routing policy, and a page
                        that painted drift red would be asserting a rule the framework does not have.
                        <span class="font-mono">unknown</span> is its own count rather than being folded
                        into either side: a run carrying no <span class="font-mono">routed</span> flag did
                        not route correctly and did not drift — it said nothing.
                    </p>
                </CardFooter>
            </Card>

            @* BRD-148 / BRD-160 — measured dollars only. No rate card reaches this page. *@
            <Card Class="h-full" data-testid="effort-cost">
                <CardHeader>
                    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
                        <div class="min-w-0">
                            <CardTitle Class="text-base">Measured spend by harness</CardTitle>
                            <CardDescription>Provider-reported dollars only</CardDescription>
                        </div>
                        <span class="tflens-stat-chip tflens-accent-2 shrink-0">
                            <LucideIcon Name="dollar-sign" Size="16" />
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </CardHeader>
                <CardContent Class="pt-0">
                    <div class="tflens-table">
                        <DataTable TData="CostRow"
                                   Data="@CostRows"
                                   ShowToolbar="false"
                                   ShowPagination="false"
                                   InitialPageSize="20"
                                   AriaLabel="Measured spend by harness"
                                   data-testid="effort-cost-table">
                            <Columns>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="CostRow" TValue="string"
                                                 Property="@(aRow => aRow.Harness)" Header="Harness">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                        @* `?` is the engine's own key for a run whose harness was not
                                           detected. It keeps its row rather than being folded into
                                           another harness's — a dollar figure attributed to the wrong
                                           harness is worse than one attributed to none. *@
                                        <span class="font-mono @(vRow.IsDetected ? string.Empty : "text-muted-foreground")">@vRow.Label</span>
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="CostRow" TValue="int"
                                                 Property="@(aRow => aRow.Records)" Header="Records"
                                                 CellClass="text-right">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                        <span class="tabular-nums" title="runs detected on this harness">@CountText(vRow.Records)</span>
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                                <DataTableColumn TData="CostRow" TValue="string"
                                                 Property="@(aRow => aRow.Usd)" Header="Measured USD"
                                                 CellClass="text-right">
                                    <CellTemplate Context="vRow">
                                        @if (vRow.HasMeasurement)
                                        {
                                            <b class="tabular-nums" title="@vRow.Basis"
                                               data-testid="@($"cost-{vRow.Harness}")">@vRow.Usd</b>
                                        }
                                        else
                                        {
                                            <span class="tabular-nums text-muted-foreground"
                                                  title="no provider cost recorded"
                                                  data-testid="@($"cost-{vRow.Harness}")">@vRow.Usd</span>
                                        }
                                    </CellTemplate>
                                </DataTableColumn>
                            </Columns>
                        </DataTable>
                    </div>
                </CardContent>
                <CardFooter Class="tflens-card-note">
                    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
                        A dash is <b>“no provider cost recorded”</b>, never
                        <span class="font-mono">$0.00</span> and never “free”. <b>There is no rate-card
                        estimate anywhere on this page</b> — an estimated dollar beside a measured one on a
                        budgeting screen is how a plausible wrong number gets quoted. Estimates live on
                        <a class="tflens-link" href="/routing">Routing &amp; economics</a>, on their own
                        card, labelled as estimates. Dollars are never summed across harnesses.
                    </p>
                </CardFooter>
            </Card>
        </div>

        @* BRD-168 — the standing actor note. *@
        <p class="tflens-actor-note text-sm text-muted-foreground" data-testid="effort-actor-note">
            <LucideIcon Name="info" Size="16" />
            <span>
                No figure on this page, in the API, in the export or in parity is grouped by
                <span class="font-mono">actor</span> — there is no parameter, filter or toggle that could
                produce such a grouping.
            </span>
        </p>
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>What a value reads when there is nothing to measure at all.</summary>
    private const string Dash = "—";

    /// <summary>The period key meaning the whole history; this page's default (BRD-125's rule again).</summary>
    private const string AllHistory = "all";

    /// <summary>
    /// The day <c>subagent_runs</c>, <c>tokens_out_subagents</c> and <c>model_tokens_out</c> began to
    /// exist. A run written before it could not have been fan-out observed, permanently (SCHEMA.md §2.6).
    /// </summary>
    private const string FieldSince = "2026-08-31";

    /// <summary>The <c>tokens_scope</c> a run declared when it computed no window.</summary>
    private const string NoneScope = "none";

    /// <summary>
    /// The engine's key for a run that carried no <c>tokens_scope</c> field at all.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// <see cref="PhaseMetrics.AbsentScope"/> is kept apart from <see cref="NoneScope"/> by the engine
    /// rather than folded into it, so this card keeps them apart too. Both are excluded from every token
    /// figure — that is one fact — but "the run said none" and "the run said nothing" are two different
    /// records, and collapsing them here would put a spelling of the exclusion on screen that the data
    /// does not have.
    /// </remarks>
    private const string AbsentScope = "absent";

    /// <summary>The period choices, all history first because it is the default.</summary>
    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<PeriodOption> PeriodOptions =
    [
        new PeriodOption(AllHistory, "All history (default)", null, "all history"),
        new PeriodOption("7", "Last 7 days", 7, "last 7 days"),
        new PeriodOption("30", "Last 30 days", 30, "last 30 days"),
        new PeriodOption("90", "Last 90 days", 90, "last 90 days")
    ];

    /// <summary>The token scopes in the order the approved design lists them.</summary>
    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<string> ScopeOrder =
        ["tree", "conversation", "main", NoneScope, AbsentScope];

    /// <summary>What each <c>tokens_scope</c> bucket means, in the design's own words.</summary>
    private static readonly IReadOnlyDictionary<string, string> ScopeMeanings =
        new Dictionary<string, string>(StringComparer.Ordinal)
        {
            ["tree"] = "main thread and child transcripts read",
            ["conversation"] = "main thread only",
            ["main"] = "main thread only",
            [NoneScope] = "declared none — no token figures exist for these runs (tokens_unmeasured_n)",
            [AbsentScope] = "carried no tokens_scope at all — no token figures exist for these runs (tokens_unmeasured_n)"
        };

    private IReadOnlyList<RunRecord> objAllRuns = [];
    private PhaseEffortAnalysis objPhases = PhaseEffortAnalysis.Empty;
    private readonly HashSet<string> objOpenPhases = new(StringComparer.Ordinal);

    private bool objIsLoaded;
    private bool objIsRoutingByPhaseOpen;
    private string? objLoadError;
    private int? objUserId;
    private string? objLoadedFramework;
    private string objPeriod = AllHistory;

    /// <summary>The signed-in principal, cascaded by <c>AddCascadingAuthenticationState</c>.</summary>
    [CascadingParameter]
    private Task<AuthenticationState>? AuthenticationStateTask { get; set; }

    /// <summary>True when the header Framework switch is on the Playbook axis (REQ-UI-010, ADR-016).</summary>
    private bool IsPlaybook => objPreferences.Framework == FrameworkNames.Playbook;

    /// <summary>The one line under the heading, which says which framework state the reader is looking at.</summary>
    private string Subtitle =>
        IsPlaybook
            ? "Playbook axis — phase efficiency, read from the imported execution events rather than from runs.jsonl"
            : "How much time and how many tokens went into each command phase — with which model, and how many "
              + "subagents it actually spun up";

    /// <summary>What the empty state says, which depends on the window the reader chose.</summary>
    private string EmptyDescription =>
        Period.Days is null
            ? "No live run records have been imported for this framework yet. Backfilled rows are excluded "
              + "from every figure on this page by design."
            : $"No live run record falls inside the {Period.Badge}. Widen the window, or switch back to all history.";

    /// <summary>The selected period, resolved back to its option.</summary>
    private PeriodOption Period =>
        PeriodOptions.FirstOrDefault(aOption => aOption.Key == objPeriod) ?? PeriodOptions[0];

    /// <summary>The badge beside the period select, so the window is stated even when the select is closed.</summary>
    private string PeriodLabel => Period.Badge;

    /// <summary>The label the closed select trigger shows for a period key (TR-020).</summary>
    /// <param name="aKey">The period key currently bound.</param>
    /// <returns>The option's label, or the key itself when it names no option.</returns>
    private static string PeriodTextOf(string aKey) =>
        PeriodOptions.FirstOrDefault(aOption => aOption.Key == aKey)?.Label ?? aKey;

    /// <summary>Runs carrying a usable token window — the divisor of every token figure (BRD-146).</summary>
    private int TokensMeasuredRuns => objPhases.Phases.Sum(aRow => aRow.TokensMeasuredN);

    /// <summary>Runs excluded from every token figure; displayed, never added into one.</summary>
    private int TokensUnmeasuredRuns => objPhases.Phases.Sum(aRow => aRow.TokensUnmeasuredN);

    /// <summary>Runs carrying a non-zero <c>duration_s</c> — the wall-clock block's own denominator.</summary>
    private int TimedRuns => objPhases.Phases.Sum(aRow => aRow.Duration.TimedN);

    /// <summary>The phase with the largest measured output; the engine already orders by it.</summary>
    private PhaseEffortRow? Heaviest => objPhases.Phases.Count == 0 ? null : objPhases.Phases[0];

    /// <summary>The heaviest phase's command, or the dash when there is no phase at all.</summary>
    private string HeaviestCmd => Heaviest?.Cmd ?? Dash;

    /// <summary>The heaviest phase's sub-line — its two shares and its run count.</summary>
    private string HeaviestSummary =>
        Heaviest is { } vRow
            ? $"{vRow.ShareOfTokensOut} of all output tokens · {vRow.ShareOfDuration} of wall clock · "
              + $"{CountText(vRow.Runs)} runs"
            : "no phase has recorded a run in this window";

    /// <summary>Every run that carried a routing outcome of any kind, including none at all.</summary>
    private int RoutingTotal =>
        objPhases.Phases.Sum(aRow => aRow.Routing.Routed + aRow.Routing.Drifted + aRow.Routing.Unknown);

    /// <summary>
    /// The token-window buckets, in the design's order, with any producer scope the design did not
    /// anticipate appended rather than dropped.
    /// </summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<ScopeRow> ScopeRows
    {
        get
        {
            var vCounts = objPhases.ScopeCoverage
                .ToDictionary(aPair => aPair.Key, aPair => aPair.Value, StringComparer.Ordinal);

            var vRows = ScopeOrder
                .Select(aScope => new ScopeRow(
                    aScope == AbsentScope ? "tokens_scope: (absent)" : $"tokens_scope: {aScope}",
                    vCounts.TryGetValue(aScope, out var vCount) ? vCount : 0,
                    ScopeMeanings[aScope],
                    aScope is NoneScope or AbsentScope,
                    aScope))
                .ToList();

            // A scope the approved design has no row for is shown rather than silently discarded: an
            // exclusion the reader cannot see is indistinguishable from a bug (BRD-121's rule again).
            vRows.AddRange(vCounts
                .Where(aPair => !ScopeOrder.Contains(aPair.Key, StringComparer.Ordinal))
                .OrderByDescending(aPair => aPair.Value)
                .Select(aPair => new ScopeRow(
                    $"tokens_scope: {aPair.Key}",
                    aPair.Value,
                    "a scope this screen has no standing description for",
                    false,
                    aPair.Key)));

            return vRows;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Fan-out observation and its two exclusions — three rows that are never pooled into two (BRD-147).
    /// </summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<ExclusionRow> ExclusionRows
    {
        get
        {
            var vNotTree = objPhases.Phases.Sum(aRow => aRow.Fanout.UnobservedNotTree);
            var vPredatesField = objPhases.Phases.Sum(aRow => aRow.Fanout.UnobservedPredatesField);

            return
            [
                new ExclusionRow(
                    "Observed",
                    "tokens_scope == \"tree\" and subagent_runs != null",
                    objPhases.FanoutObservedN,
                    Percent(objPhases.FanoutObservedN, objPhases.RunsLive),
                    "tflens-fill-2",
                    true,
                    "observed"),
                new ExclusionRow(
                    "unobserved_not_tree",
                    "We did not look. The window was main, conversation or none, so no child transcript was ever read",
                    vNotTree,
                    Percent(vNotTree, objPhases.RunsLive),
                    "tflens-fill-4",
                    false,
                    "not-tree"),
                new ExclusionRow(
                    "unobserved_predates_field",
                    $"We could not have looked. Tree scope, but written before subagent_runs existed ({FieldSince})",
                    vPredatesField,
                    Percent(vPredatesField, objPhases.RunsLive),
                    "tflens-fill-5",
                    false,
                    "predates-field")
            ];
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The phase table's rows, in the engine's own heaviest-output-first order (REQ-UI-047).</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<PhaseTableRow> PhaseTableRows =>
        objPhases.Phases.Select(aRow => new PhaseTableRow(
            aRow.Cmd,
            KeyOf(aRow.Cmd),
            aRow.Runs,
            PhaseTotalText(aRow),
            SecondsText(aRow.Duration.MedianSeconds),
            aRow.ShareOfDuration,
            TokenTotalText(aRow, aRow.Tokens.Out),
            aRow.TokensMeasuredN == 0 ? "no token window on any run in this phase" : ExactTokenText(aRow.Tokens.Out),
            aRow.ShareOfTokensOut,
            $"{aRow.TokensMeasuredN} of {aRow.Runs}",
            FanoutCell(aRow.Fanout),
            aRow.Fanout.IsObserved)).ToList();

    /// <summary>The three routing outcomes, in the design's order (REQ-UI-049).</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<RoutingRow> RoutingRows =>
    [
        new RoutingRow(
            "routed",
            objPhases.Phases.Sum(aRow => aRow.Routing.Routed),
            "the model that ran is the one the routing table names",
            "tflens-badge-success",
            "tflens-fill-2"),
        new RoutingRow(
            "drifted",
            objPhases.Phases.Sum(aRow => aRow.Routing.Drifted),
            "a different model ran — drift made visible, not a failure",
            "tflens-badge-info",
            "tflens-fill-1"),
        new RoutingRow(
            "unknown",
            objPhases.Phases.Sum(aRow => aRow.Routing.Unknown),
            "no declared route on the record",
            string.Empty,
            "tflens-fill-muted")
    ];

    /// <summary>
    /// Measured dollars per harness — never pooled across harnesses, never priced from a rate card.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// BRD-148 / BRD-160. A harness that measured nothing keeps its row and reads <c>—</c>: dropping it
    /// would make an unmeasured harness indistinguishable from an absent one, and a <c>$0.00</c> would
    /// state that it ran for free. Claude Code and Codex carry <c>cost_usd: null</c> permanently.
    /// </remarks>
    private IReadOnlyList<CostRow> CostRows
    {
        get
        {
            var vRuns = objPhases.Phases
                .SelectMany(aRow => aRow.Harnesses)
                .GroupBy(aPair => aPair.Key, StringComparer.Ordinal)
                .ToDictionary(aGroup => aGroup.Key, aGroup => aGroup.Sum(aPair => aPair.Value), StringComparer.Ordinal);

            var vCosts = objPhases.Phases
                .SelectMany(aRow => aRow.CostUsdByHarness)
                .GroupBy(aCost => aCost.Harness, StringComparer.Ordinal)
                .ToDictionary(
                    aGroup => aGroup.Key,
                    aGroup => (Usd: aGroup.Sum(aCost => aCost.Usd), Records: aGroup.Sum(aCost => aCost.Records)),
                    StringComparer.Ordinal);

            var vHarnesses = vRuns.Keys.Union(vCosts.Keys, StringComparer.Ordinal);

            return vHarnesses
                .Select(aHarness =>
                {
                    var vHasCost = vCosts.TryGetValue(aHarness, out var vCost);

                    return new CostRow(
                        aHarness,
                        vRuns.TryGetValue(aHarness, out var vCount) ? vCount : 0,
                        vHasCost ? vCost.Usd.ToString("C2", CultureInfo.GetCultureInfo("en-US")) : Dash,
                        vHasCost,
                        vHasCost
                            ? $"Σ cost_usd over {vCost.Records} measured records on {aHarness}"
                            : "no provider cost recorded");
                })
                .OrderByDescending(aRow => aRow.HasMeasurement)
                .ThenByDescending(aRow => aRow.Records)
                .ThenBy(aRow => aRow.Harness, StringComparer.Ordinal)
                .ToList();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Subscribes to the shell so a sync or a framework change re-queries this page.</summary>
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        objShellState.Changed += OnShellChanged;
        objPreferences.Changed += OnShellChanged;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Resolves the signed-in user and loads the run records for the selected framework.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// ADR-016 — the framework is a query, never a display filter, so a change of axis re-reads the
    /// store rather than filtering figures already on screen.
    /// </remarks>
    /// <returns>A task that completes when the page has its figures or its error.</returns>
    protected override async Task OnParametersSetAsync()
    {
        if (AuthenticationStateTask is null)
        {
            return;
        }

        if (objUserId is null)
        {
            var vState = await AuthenticationStateTask;
            objUserId = ShellIdentity.UserId(vState.User);

            if (objUserId is null)
            {
                objIsLoaded = true;
                return;
            }
        }

        if (objLoadedFramework != objPreferences.Framework)
        {
            await LoadAsync();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Reads every run record for the signed-in user on the selected framework.
    /// </summary>
    /// <returns>A task that completes when the records are in hand and the block is computed.</returns>
    private async Task LoadAsync()
    {
        if (objUserId is null)
        {
            return;
        }

        objIsLoaded = false;
        objLoadedFramework = objPreferences.Framework;

        try
        {
            objAllRuns = await objStore.ReadRunsAsync(objUserId.Value, objPreferences.Framework);
            objLoadError = null;
        }
        catch (Exception vEx)
        {
            objAllRuns = [];
            objLoadError = vEx.Message;
        }

        Recompute();
        objIsLoaded = true;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Re-runs the phase-effort engine over the records inside the selected period.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// The period narrows the <b>record set</b> and hands it to <see cref="PhaseMetrics.Compute"/>, so
    /// every guard — the live-only filter, the token-window predicate, the fan-out observation predicate,
    /// the MIN_N floor — is applied by the same code that computes the unfiltered view rather than by a
    /// second copy of the rules living in a Razor file (REQ-NFR-013).
    /// </remarks>
    private void Recompute()
    {
        var vCutoff = Period.Days is { } vDays
            ? DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.AddDays(-vDays)
            : (DateTimeOffset?)null;

        var vRuns = objAllRuns.Where(aRun => IsInPeriod(aRun.Ts, vCutoff)).ToList();

        objPhases = PhaseMetrics.Compute(vRuns);

        // REQ-UI-048 — one phase open by default, and it is the heaviest, because that is the row a
        // reader opened this page to look at. A phase that leaves the window keeps no stale open state.
        objOpenPhases.RemoveWhere(aCmd => !objPhases.Phases.Any(aRow => aRow.Cmd == aCmd));

        if (objOpenPhases.Count == 0 && objPhases.Phases.Count > 0)
        {
            objOpenPhases.Add(objPhases.Phases[0].Cmd);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Decides whether a record's timestamp falls inside the selected window.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="aTs">The record's ISO-8601 timestamp.</param>
    /// <param name="aCutoff">The oldest instant the window admits, or <c>null</c> for all history.</param>
    /// <returns><c>true</c> when the record is in the window; an unparseable timestamp is kept.</returns>
    private static bool IsInPeriod(string? aTs, DateTimeOffset? aCutoff)
    {
        if (aCutoff is null)
        {
            return true;
        }

        // A timestamp TfLens cannot parse is kept rather than dropped: silently removing a record from a
        // count because its own clock string is odd would understate every figure with no visible reason.
        return !DateTimeOffset.TryParse(
                   aTs,
                   CultureInfo.InvariantCulture,
                   DateTimeStyles.RoundtripKind,
                   out var vWhen)
               || vWhen >= aCutoff.Value;
    }

    /// <summary>Re-computes the page for the new window (REQ-UI-045).</summary>
    /// <param name="aPeriod">The period key the reader chose.</param>
    /// <returns>A completed task; the recompute is synchronous over already-loaded records.</returns>
    private Task OnPeriodChangedAsync(string aPeriod)
    {
        objPeriod = aPeriod;
        Recompute();
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    /// <summary>Opens or closes one phase's detail (REQ-UI-048).</summary>
    /// <param name="aCmd">The phase's command.</param>
    /// <param name="aIsOpen">Whether the disclosure is now open.</param>
    private void OnPhaseToggled(string aCmd, bool aIsOpen)
    {
        if (aIsOpen)
        {
            objOpenPhases.Add(aCmd);
        }
        else
        {
            objOpenPhases.Remove(aCmd);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>A stable, id-safe key for a command, used for this page's test ids.</summary>
    /// <param name="aCmd">The framework command.</param>
    /// <returns>The command with anything but a letter, digit or dash replaced by a dash.</returns>
    private static string KeyOf(string aCmd) =>
        string.Concat(aCmd.Select(aChar => char.IsLetterOrDigit(aChar) || aChar == '-' ? aChar : '-'));

    /// <summary>The trigger line's one-line summary of a phase.</summary>
    /// <param name="aRow">The phase.</param>
    /// <returns>Runs, wall clock and measured output, as the design writes it.</returns>
    private static string TriggerSummary(PhaseEffortRow aRow) =>
        $"{CountText(aRow.Runs)} runs · {PhaseTotalText(aRow)} · {TokenTotalText(aRow, aRow.Tokens.Out)} output";

    /// <summary>
    /// Renders one of a phase's four token totals, or the dash when no run in it carried a window.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// The engine reports <see cref="PhaseTokens.Zero"/> for a phase nothing could be measured in,
    /// because a sum over no records is arithmetically zero — but on screen a bare <c>0</c> reads as
    /// "this phase produced no output" when the truth is "no run here carried a token window". The
    /// phase keeps its row, as the UI design requires, and its token cells read <c>—</c>. The
    /// <c>Measured</c> column beside it says <c>0 of N</c>, which is the fact.
    /// </remarks>
    /// <param name="aRow">The phase.</param>
    /// <param name="aTotal">The total to render.</param>
    /// <returns>The compact count, or the dash.</returns>
    private static string TokenTotalText(PhaseEffortRow aRow, long aTotal) =>
        aRow.TokensMeasuredN == 0 ? Dash : TokenText(aTotal);

    /// <summary>
    /// The observation badge on a phase's trigger.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// ADR-026 — a phase nothing could be observed in reads <c>not observed</c>. It never reads
    /// <c>0 observed</c>, which invites the reader to hear "we looked and found none".
    /// </remarks>
    /// <param name="aRow">The phase.</param>
    /// <returns>The badge text.</returns>
    private static string ObservationBadge(PhaseEffortRow aRow) =>
        aRow.Fanout.IsObserved ? $"{aRow.Fanout.ObservedN} of {aRow.Runs} observed" : "not observed";

    /// <summary>The phase table's fan-out cell.</summary>
    /// <param name="aFanout">The phase's observation.</param>
    /// <returns><c>n observed</c>, or the literal <c>not observed</c> — never a zero.</returns>
    private static string FanoutCell(FanoutObservation aFanout) =>
        aFanout.IsObserved ? $"{aFanout.ObservedN} observed" : "not observed";

    /// <summary>
    /// The sentence under the fan-out band's heading, which states the coverage before any number.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="aRow">The phase.</param>
    /// <returns>The coverage sentence, naming both exclusions separately (BRD-147, BRD-149).</returns>
    private static string FanoutCoverageSentence(PhaseEffortRow aRow)
    {
        var vExclusions = $"{aRow.Fanout.UnobservedNotTree} unobserved_not_tree, "
            + $"{aRow.Fanout.UnobservedPredatesField} unobserved_predates_field";

        return aRow.Fanout.IsObserved
            ? $"Every number below is computed over those {aRow.Fanout.ObservedN} runs only. The rest were "
              + $"not observed — {vExclusions} — and none of them contributes a zero."
            : $"No run here could be observed — {vExclusions} — so this phase reports no fan-out at all. "
              + "That is an absence of observation, not a measurement of zero.";
    }

    /// <summary>The declared-vs-measured sentence, which never reconciles the two (BRD-149).</summary>
    /// <param name="aRow">The phase.</param>
    /// <returns>What the agents declared and what the harness counted.</returns>
    private static string DeclaredVersusMeasured(PhaseEffortRow aRow)
    {
        var vDeclared = aRow.SubagentsDeclared.Count == 0
            ? "The runs declared no subagent kinds at all."
            : "The agents typed subagents: ["
              + string.Join(", ", aRow.SubagentsDeclared.Select(aKind => $"\"{aKind.Key}\""))
              + $"] — {aRow.SubagentsDeclared.Count} kinds.";

        var vMeasured = aRow.Fanout.IsObserved
            ? $"The harness counted {aRow.Fanout.SpawnsTotal} spawns over the runs it could observe."
            : "The harness observed no run here, so it counted nothing — which is not the same as counting none.";

        return $"{vDeclared} {vMeasured}";
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The mean-beside-median sentence, which says what the pair means rather than repeating it.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// A mean far above the median means one long run dominates the phase, which is the most
    /// decision-relevant thing on the token band — and the reason the two sit side by side.
    /// </remarks>
    /// <param name="aRow">The phase.</param>
    /// <returns>The sentence.</returns>
    private static string MeanVersusMedian(PhaseEffortRow aRow)
    {
        // ADR-007 — the number is read through TryGetValue, the only accessor a Figure has. Below the
        // MIN_N floor it carries none at all, and this sentence says so rather than inventing a gap.
        if (aRow.TokensOutMedian is not { } vMedian
            || vMedian <= 0
            || !aRow.TokensOutPerRun.Tokens.TryGetValue(out var vMean))
        {
            return "A mean far above the median would say one long run dominates the phase rather than "
                + "that a typical run costs the mean; this phase has no pair to compare yet.";
        }

        var vGap = Math.Round(((vMean - vMedian) / vMedian) * 100d, MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero);

        if (Math.Abs(vGap) < 1d)
        {
            return $"The mean output ({TokenFromDouble(vMean)}) sits on the median "
                + $"({TokenFromDouble(vMedian)}), so no single run dominates this phase.";
        }

        var vDirection = vGap > 0 ? "above" : "below";

        return $"The mean output ({TokenFromDouble(vMean)}) is {Math.Abs(vGap).ToString("0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)}% "
            + $"{vDirection} the median ({TokenFromDouble(vMedian)}), which says one long run dominates this "
            + "phase rather than that a typical run costs the mean.";
    }

    /// <summary>The excluded-runs sentence under the token band.</summary>
    /// <param name="aRow">The phase.</param>
    /// <returns>How many runs carry no window, or a line saying every run did.</returns>
    private static string UnmeasuredNote(PhaseEffortRow aRow) =>
        aRow.TokensUnmeasuredN == 0
            ? "Every run in this phase carried a token window."
            : $"{aRow.TokensUnmeasuredN} runs are excluded from every figure in this band — they carry no "
              + "token window.";

    /// <summary>The timed-runs sentence under the time band.</summary>
    /// <param name="aRow">The phase.</param>
    /// <returns>How many of the phase's runs were actually timed.</returns>
    private static string TimedRunsNote(PhaseEffortRow aRow) =>
        aRow.Duration.TimedN == aRow.Runs
            ? $"All {aRow.Runs} runs were timed."
            : $"Timed on {aRow.Duration.TimedN} of {aRow.Runs} runs; the rest carry no duration_s.";

    /// <summary>
    /// Says how much of a phase's per-model weight rests on measured splits rather than on labels.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// BRD-150 — a row resting largely on dominant-model labels is a weaker observation than one resting
    /// on <c>model_tokens_out</c> splits, so the two counts are shown rather than blended invisibly.
    /// </remarks>
    /// <param name="aRow">The phase.</param>
    /// <returns>The sentence.</returns>
    private static string ModelSourceNote(PhaseEffortRow aRow)
    {
        var vFromSplit = aRow.Models.Sum(aModel => aModel.RunsFromSplit);
        var vFromLabel = aRow.Models.Sum(aModel => aModel.RunsFromLabel);

        if (vFromLabel == 0)
        {
            return $"All {vFromSplit} contributions here come from a measured split.";
        }

        if (vFromSplit == 0)
        {
            return $"None of these {vFromLabel} contributions comes from a measured split — every one is "
                + "read off the dominant model label on a run that carried none, which is the weaker "
                + "observation and is counted as such.";
        }

        return $"{vFromSplit} contributions come from a measured split and {vFromLabel} from a dominant "
            + "model label on a run that carried no split — counted apart, because they are not equally "
            + "strong observations.";
    }

    /// <summary>The spawn median and max, or the dash when nothing was observed.</summary>
    /// <param name="aFanout">The phase's observation.</param>
    /// <returns><c>4 · 9</c>, or the dash on either half that has no value.</returns>
    private static string SpawnsMedianAndMax(FanoutObservation aFanout)
    {
        var vMedian = aFanout.Spawns is { } vValue
            ? vValue.ToString("0.##", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)
            : Dash;

        var vMax = aFanout.SpawnsMax is { } vPeak
            ? vPeak.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)
            : Dash;

        return $"{vMedian} · {vMax}";
    }

    /// <summary>A phase's total wall clock, or the dash when no run in it was timed.</summary>
    /// <param name="aRow">The phase.</param>
    /// <returns>The formatted total, or the dash.</returns>
    private static string PhaseTotalText(PhaseEffortRow aRow) =>
        aRow.Duration.TimedN == 0 ? Dash : DurationText(aRow.Duration.TotalSeconds);

    /// <summary>Formats an optional second count, which is <c>null</c> when nothing was timed.</summary>
    /// <param name="aSeconds">The seconds, or <c>null</c>.</param>
    /// <returns>The formatted duration, or the dash — never a zero.</returns>
    private static string SecondsText(double? aSeconds) =>
        aSeconds is { } vValue ? DurationText((long)Math.Round(vValue, MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero)) : Dash;

    /// <summary>Formats an optional second count, which is <c>null</c> when nothing was timed.</summary>
    /// <param name="aSeconds">The seconds, or <c>null</c>.</param>
    /// <returns>The formatted duration, or the dash — never a zero.</returns>
    private static string SecondsText(long? aSeconds) =>
        aSeconds is { } vValue ? DurationText(vValue) : Dash;

    /// <summary>
    /// Formats a wall-clock total in the approved design's notation — <c>21h 40m</c>, <c>42m</c>, <c>12s</c>.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="aSeconds">The duration in seconds.</param>
    /// <returns>The formatted duration.</returns>
    private static string DurationText(long aSeconds)
    {
        if (aSeconds <= 0L)
        {
            return "0s";
        }

        var vHours = aSeconds / 3600L;
        var vMinutes = (aSeconds % 3600L) / 60L;

        if (vHours > 0L)
        {
            return $"{vHours.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)}h "
                + $"{vMinutes.ToString("00", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)}m";
        }

        return vMinutes > 0L
            ? $"{vMinutes.ToString("0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)}m"
            : $"{aSeconds.ToString("0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)}s";
    }

    /// <summary>Renders a whole count in the grouped form every table on this page uses.</summary>
    /// <param name="aValue">The count.</param>
    /// <returns>The grouped number.</returns>
    private static string CountText(long aValue) => aValue.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);

    /// <summary>
    /// Renders a token count in the approved design's compact notation — <c>24.2M</c>, <c>62k</c>.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Abbreviating is a presentation choice and never the only rendering: the phase table carries the
    /// exact count as the cell's <c>title</c>, and the export path never passes through here at all, so
    /// key-for-key parity is untouched.
    /// </remarks>
    /// <param name="aValue">The token count.</param>
    /// <returns>The compact count.</returns>
    private static string TokenText(long aValue)
    {
        var vMagnitude = Math.Abs(aValue);

        if (vMagnitude >= 1_000_000_000L)
        {
            return (aValue / 1_000_000_000d).ToString("0.0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) + "B";
        }

        if (vMagnitude >= 1_000_000L)
        {
            return (aValue / 1_000_000d).ToString("0.0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) + "M";
        }

        if (vMagnitude >= 1_000L)
        {
            return (aValue / 1_000d).ToString("0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) + "k";
        }

        return aValue.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
    }

    /// <summary>The exact token count an abbreviated cell keeps as its native tooltip.</summary>
    /// <param name="aValue">The token count.</param>
    /// <returns>The grouped count with its noun.</returns>
    private static string ExactTokenText(long aValue) =>
        aValue.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) + " tokens";

    /// <summary>Renders an optional per-run token figure, which is <c>null</c> when nothing was measured.</summary>
    /// <param name="aValue">The figure, or <c>null</c>.</param>
    /// <returns>The compact count, or the dash — never a zero.</returns>
    private static string TokenFromDouble(double? aValue) =>
        aValue is { } vValue
            ? TokenText((long)Math.Round(vValue, MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero))
            : Dash;

    /// <summary>
    /// A share as a 0..100 progress value.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="aPart">The numerator.</param>
    /// <param name="aWhole">The denominator.</param>
    /// <returns>The percentage, or zero width when there is no denominator to take a share of.</returns>
    private static double Percent(long aPart, long aWhole) =>
        aWhole <= 0L ? 0d : (aPart / (double)aWhole) * 100d;

    /// <summary>
    /// A share as the whole percentage the design prints beside a bar.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="aPart">The numerator.</param>
    /// <param name="aWhole">The denominator.</param>
    /// <returns>
    /// A percentage such as <c>7%</c>, or the dash when the denominator is zero — a share taken from
    /// nothing is not <c>0%</c>, it is a figure that does not exist.
    /// </returns>
    private static string PercentText(long aPart, long aWhole) =>
        aWhole <= 0L
            ? Dash
            : Math.Round((aPart / (double)aWhole) * 100d, MidpointRounding.AwayFromZero)
                .ToString("0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture) + "%";

    /// <summary>Re-queries when the workspace or the chosen provenance axis changes under the page.</summary>
    private void OnShellChanged() => InvokeAsync(async () =>
    {
        objLoadedFramework = null;
        await LoadAsync();
        StateHasChanged();
    });

    /// <summary>Unsubscribes so the circuit does not leak a handler per navigation.</summary>
    public void Dispose()
    {
        objShellState.Changed -= OnShellChanged;
        objPreferences.Changed -= OnShellChanged;
    }

    /// <summary>One period choice in the header filter.</summary>
    /// <param name="Key">The bound value.</param>
    /// <param name="Label">What the option reads in the list and on the closed trigger.</param>
    /// <param name="Days">How many days back the window reaches, or <c>null</c> for all history.</param>
    /// <param name="Badge">The short form shown on the badge beside the select.</param>
    private sealed record PeriodOption(string Key, string Label, int? Days, string Badge);

    /// <summary>One <c>tokens_scope</c> bucket on the token-window denominator card.</summary>
    /// <param name="Scope">The bucket's label, as the producer spells the scope.</param>
    /// <param name="Runs">Live runs in the bucket.</param>
    /// <param name="Meaning">What the bucket means, in one line.</param>
    /// <param name="IsUnmeasured">True on the <c>none</c>/absent row, which no token figure includes.</param>
    /// <param name="TestKey">The stable test id fragment for the row's count.</param>
    private sealed record ScopeRow(string Scope, int Runs, string Meaning, bool IsUnmeasured, string TestKey);

    /// <summary>One row of the fan-out observation card — the observed set, or one of its two exclusions.</summary>
    /// <param name="Label">The row's name.</param>
    /// <param name="Meaning">What the row means, in the design's own words.</param>
    /// <param name="Runs">Live runs in the row.</param>
    /// <param name="Percent">The row's share of live runs, as a 0..100 bar value.</param>
    /// <param name="FillClass">Which chart colour the bar is painted with.</param>
    /// <param name="IsObservedRow">True on the observed row, which is the only measured one.</param>
    /// <param name="TestKey">The stable test id fragment for the row's count.</param>
    private sealed record ExclusionRow(
        string Label,
        string Meaning,
        int Runs,
        double Percent,
        string FillClass,
        bool IsObservedRow,
        string TestKey)
    {
        /// <summary>The row's count as text, which is also the column's sort key.</summary>
        public string Text => Runs.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
    }

    /// <summary>One row of the command-phase table.</summary>
    /// <param name="Cmd">The framework command.</param>
    /// <param name="Key">The id-safe form of <paramref name="Cmd"/>, for test ids.</param>
    /// <param name="Runs">Live runs in the phase.</param>
    /// <param name="WallClock">Summed duration over the timed runs, or the dash.</param>
    /// <param name="Median">The median timed run, or the dash.</param>
    /// <param name="ShareOfDuration">The oracle's own share string, rendered unaltered.</param>
    /// <param name="TokensOut">Measured output tokens, compactly.</param>
    /// <param name="TokensOutExact">The same total, exactly, as the cell's tooltip.</param>
    /// <param name="ShareOfTokensOut">The oracle's own share string, rendered unaltered.</param>
    /// <param name="Measured">
    /// <c>n of N</c> — the column BRD-151 requires, never a footnote.
    /// </param>
    /// <param name="Fanout"><c>n observed</c>, or the literal <c>not observed</c>.</param>
    /// <param name="IsFanoutObserved">Whether any run in the phase could be observed at all.</param>
    private sealed record PhaseTableRow(
        string Cmd,
        string Key,
        int Runs,
        string WallClock,
        string Median,
        string ShareOfDuration,
        string TokensOut,
        string TokensOutExact,
        string ShareOfTokensOut,
        string Measured,
        string Fanout,
        bool IsFanoutObserved);

    /// <summary>One routing outcome.</summary>
    /// <param name="Outcome"><c>routed</c>, <c>drifted</c> or <c>unknown</c>.</param>
    /// <param name="Runs">Runs with that outcome.</param>
    /// <param name="Meaning">What the outcome means, in one line.</param>
    /// <param name="ToneClass">
    /// The badge tone. <c>drifted</c> is <b>info</b> and never destructive: drift is observed, never
    /// enforced (REQ-UI-049).
    /// </param>
    /// <param name="FillClass">Which chart colour the share bar is painted with.</param>
    private sealed record RoutingRow(string Outcome, int Runs, string Meaning, string ToneClass, string FillClass);

    /// <summary>One harness's measured spend.</summary>
    /// <param name="Harness">The detected harness.</param>
    /// <param name="Records">Runs detected on it.</param>
    /// <param name="Usd">The measured total, or the dash — never <c>$0.00</c> and never "free".</param>
    /// <param name="HasMeasurement">Whether any record on this harness reported a provider cost.</param>
    /// <param name="Basis">What the figure was summed over, kept as the cell's tooltip.</param>
    private sealed record CostRow(string Harness, int Records, string Usd, bool HasMeasurement, string Basis)
    {
        /// <summary>True unless this is the engine's <c>?</c> bucket for an undetected harness.</summary>
        public bool IsDetected => !string.Equals(Harness, PhaseMetrics.Unknown, StringComparison.Ordinal);

        /// <summary>How the harness cell reads; the undetected bucket says so in words.</summary>
        public string Label => IsDetected ? Harness : "harness not detected";
    }
}
